---
/**
 * LLM / AI server sizing calculator.
 * Markup is static; behaviour is wired in src/scripts/llm-calculator via delegated events.
 */
import modelsData from '../data/llm-calculator-models.json';
---

<div id="calcRoot" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10 lg:py-14 min-w-0">

  <!-- Header -->
  <div class="text-center mb-10">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white text-brand-teal border border-brand-teal/30 rounded-full px-4 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] mb-5 flex-wrap justify-center">
      🏢 On-Premises · Offline AI
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl xl:text-5xl font-extrabold text-brand-forest tracking-tight mb-2 leading-tight text-wrap-balance max-w-lg mx-auto">AI Hardware Sizing Calculator</h1>
    <p class="text-brand-muted text-sm max-w-lg mx-auto leading-relaxed text-wrap-pretty">
      Answer a few questions to see how many GPUs you need and what they cost to run. You set the specs — we don't assume any prices.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Step indicator -->
  <div class="flex items-center mb-10 px-1 overflow-x-auto snap-x snap-mandatory -mx-1 pb-2" id="stepTrack" role="tablist" aria-label="Calculator steps">
    <div class="step-dot active shrink-0 snap-start" id="sd1" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-label="Step 1: Model">1</div>
    <div class="step-line shrink-0" id="sl1"></div>
    <div class="step-dot shrink-0" id="sd2" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-label="Step 2: Prompts">2</div>
    <div class="step-line shrink-0" id="sl2"></div>
    <div class="step-dot shrink-0" id="sd3" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-label="Step 3: Users">3</div>
    <div class="step-line shrink-0" id="sl3"></div>
    <div class="step-dot shrink-0" id="sd4" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-label="Step 4: Speed">4</div>
    <div class="step-line shrink-0" id="sl4"></div>
    <div class="step-dot shrink-0 snap-end" id="sd5" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-label="Step 5: GPUs">5</div>
  </div>

  <!-- STEP 1 -->
  <div id="step1" class="fade-in">
    <div class="card mb-5">
      <p class="sec-hdr">Step 1 of 5 — Pick your AI model</p>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-forest mb-1">Which AI model will you use?</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-muted text-sm mb-5">The model you pick decides most of your cost. Bigger models work better but need more memory.</p>

      <label class="field-label">Select a model</label>
      <span class="field-sub">Not sure? Llama 3.1 70B is a common choice that balances quality and cost.</span>
      <select id="modelSelect" data-action="onModelChange">
        <option value="" disabled selected>— Choose a model —</option>
        {Object.entries(modelsData).map(([key, model]) => (
          <option value={key}>{model.label}  ({model.params}B parameters)</option>
        ))}
      </select>

      <div id="modelNote" class="mt-4 hidden info-box">
        <strong class="text-brand-teal">What the model needs (from its maker):</strong>
        <div id="modelNoteText" class="mt-2 text-brand-forest/80"></div>
        <p class="note mt-2">We get these details from the model's public specs. You can change them in step 3 if you know better. (The AI holds some memory while it works — the calculator uses these details to work that out.)</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card mb-5">
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-brand-forest mb-1">How precise should the AI be?</h3>
      <p class="text-brand-muted text-sm mb-4">This sets how the AI stores numbers. More precise means better results but more memory. The guide uses: <span class="text-brand-teal font-mono">M = P × Z × 1.2</span><br/><span class="text-brand-muted">In plain terms: this number (Z) sets how much memory the model uses.</span></p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 grid-cols-1 gap-3">
        <button class="choice-btn" data-action="selPrec" data-prec="INT4" data-z="0.5">
          <div class="ct">INT4 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Z = 0.5</div>
          <div class="cd">Smallest. Slight loss in quality. Uses the least memory.</div>
        </button>
        <button class="choice-btn" data-action="selPrec" data-prec="FP8" data-z="1">
          <div class="ct">FP8 / INT8 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Z = 1</div>
          <div class="cd">Half the memory of FP16. Works on modern GPUs.</div>
        </button>
        <button class="choice-btn sel" data-action="selPrec" data-prec="FP16" data-z="2">
          <div class="ct">FP16 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Z = 2 &nbsp;✓ Recommended</div>
          <div class="cd">The standard for running AI in production. Best balance of quality and memory.</div>
        </button>
        <button class="choice-btn" data-action="selPrec" data-prec="FP32" data-z="4">
          <div class="ct">FP32 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Z = 4</div>
          <div class="cd">Highest quality. Twice the memory of FP16. For research or critical work.</div>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex justify-end mt-4">
      <button class="btn-primary min-w-[200px] sm:min-w-auto" id="s1next" data-action="goStep" data-step="2" disabled>Next: prompts and responses →</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- STEP 2 -->
  <div id="step2" class="hidden fade-in">
    <div class="card mb-5">
      <p class="sec-hdr">Step 2 of 5 — Prompts and responses</p>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-forest mb-1">How long are your prompts and responses?</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-muted text-sm mb-1">The guide calls the full length the <strong class="text-brand-forest/70">context window</strong>: your prompt plus the response. This length drives how much memory the AI holds while it works — longer prompts and responses need more memory per person.</p>
      <p class="note mb-5">A token is a short piece of text — about 4 characters. A 1,000-word document is roughly 1,333 tokens.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-2">
        <div>
          <label class="field-label">Average input tokens per request</label>
          <span class="field-sub">Your system instructions, the user's message, and any documents you include.</span>
          <div class="range-row mb-2">
            <input type="range" id="inTokR" min="100" max="100000" step="100" value="4000" data-input="syncToken" data-target="inTok" />
            <span class="range-val" id="inTokV">4,000</span>
          </div>
          <input type="number" id="inTok" value="4000" min="1" max="128000" data-input="syncSlider" data-range="inTokR" data-view="inTokV" class="mt-1" />
          <div class="flex justify-between mt-1"><span class="note">100</span><span class="note">128,000 (max Llama 3.1)</span></div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label class="field-label">Average output tokens per response</label>
          <span class="field-sub">How long the AI's reply typically is. A short answer ≈ 100–300 tokens; a full report ≈ 1,000–4,000.</span>
          <div class="range-row mb-2">
            <input type="range" id="outTokR" min="50" max="8000" step="50" value="500" data-input="syncToken" data-target="outTok" />
            <span class="range-val" id="outTokV">500</span>
          </div>
          <input type="number" id="outTok" value="500" min="1" max="8000" data-input="syncSlider" data-range="outTokR" data-view="outTokV" class="mt-1" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="info-box mt-4">
        <strong class="text-brand-teal">Total length = </strong>
        <span id="ctxWindowLive" class="text-brand-forest font-bold">4,500</span> tokens
        <span class="text-brand-muted ml-2">(your prompt plus the response — this is what the AI holds in memory)</span>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4">
        <label class="field-label mb-2">Quick presets</label>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <button class="choice-btn" data-action="setTokens" data-in="500" data-out="200"><div class="ct">Short Q&amp;A</div><div class="cd">500 in + 200 out = 700 tokens</div></button>
          <button class="choice-btn" data-action="setTokens" data-in="2000" data-out="800"><div class="ct">Document summary</div><div class="cd">2,000 in + 800 out = 2,800 tokens</div></button>
          <button class="choice-btn" data-action="setTokens" data-in="7000" data-out="1000"><div class="ct">Long document analysis</div><div class="cd">7,000 in + 1,000 out = 8,000 tokens</div></button>
          <button class="choice-btn" data-action="setTokens" data-in="60000" data-out="4000"><div class="ct">RAG / large knowledge base</div><div class="cd">60,000 in + 4,000 out = 64,000 tokens</div></button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:justify-between gap-3 mt-4">
      <button class="btn-ghost" data-action="goStep" data-step="1">← Back</button>
      <button class="btn-primary" data-action="goStep" data-step="3">Next: how many people →</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- STEP 3 -->
  <div id="step3" class="hidden fade-in">
    <div class="card mb-5">
      <p class="sec-hdr">Step 3 of 5 — Concurrent users</p>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-forest mb-1">How many concurrent users will use the AI at peak?</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-muted text-sm mb-1">Size for your busiest moment, not your average. The guide also works out your true peak from your average requests per second.</p>
      <p class="note mb-5">The guide warns: if you don't plan for peak use, each prompt can cost you more.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 mb-5">
        <div>
          <label class="field-label">Concurrent users at peak</label>
          <span class="field-sub">How many people send a request at the same moment during your busiest hour.</span>
          <div class="range-row mb-2">
            <input type="range" id="usersR" min="1" max="500" value="10" data-input="syncToken" data-target="usersN" />
            <span class="range-val" id="usersV">10</span>
          </div>
          <input type="number" id="usersN" value="10" min="1" max="10000" data-input="syncSlider" data-range="usersR" data-view="usersV" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label class="field-label">Average requests per second (RPS)</label>
          <span class="field-sub">Optional but useful: we use this to work out your peak load and your cost per prompt.</span>
          <input type="number" id="rpsAvg" value="1" min="0.01" max="1000" step="0.1" data-input="calcPoissonPeak" />
          <div id="rpsPeak" class="info-box mt-2 text-xs">Enter your requests per second to see your estimated peak.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-2">
        <button class="btn-sm mb-3" data-action="toggleArchOverride">⚙ Change advanced model details (optional)</button>
        <div id="archOverride" class="hidden">
          <div class="warn-box mb-3">These details come from the model itself and feed the memory formula: <span class="font-mono text-amber-600">M_KV = 2 × C × T_seq × L × (N_attn / g) × D_head × Z</span>.<br/><span class="text-amber-700">In plain terms: this works out the memory the AI holds while it works. The values are pre-filled from the model's public specs.</span></div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
            <div>
              <label class="field-label">Layers</label>
              <input type="number" id="ovrLayers" class="gpu-input" data-input="recalcLive" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label class="field-label">Attention heads</label>
              <input type="number" id="ovrAttnH" class="gpu-input" data-input="recalcLive" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label class="field-label">KV heads</label>
              <span class="field-sub">If your model gives a KV head count directly, enter it here. Same as attention heads for standard models; 1 for the simplest design.</span>
              <input type="number" id="ovrKvH" class="gpu-input" data-input="recalcLive" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label class="field-label">Head dimension</label>
              <input type="number" id="ovrDHead" class="gpu-input" data-input="recalcLive" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:justify-between gap-3 mt-4">
      <button class="btn-ghost" data-action="goStep" data-step="2">← Back</button>
      <button class="btn-primary" data-action="goStep" data-step="4">Next: reply speed →</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- STEP 4 -->
  <div id="step4" class="hidden fade-in">
    <div class="card mb-5">
      <p class="sec-hdr">Step 4 of 5 — Reply speed</p>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-forest mb-1">How fast does the AI need to respond?</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-muted text-sm mb-5">The guide measures two speeds that affect your hardware. Tighter limits mean the system handles fewer people at once.</p>

      <div class="info-box mb-5 text-xs">
        <strong class="text-brand-teal">Time to first word (TTFT)</strong> — how long until the first word shows up. Set by the first stage of work.<br/>
        <strong class="text-brand-teal mt-1 block">Total time for the reply (TTLT)</strong> — from sending the prompt to getting the whole response. Set by the final stage of work.
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-5">
        <div>
          <label class="field-label">Max time to first word (TTFT), in seconds</label>
          <span class="field-sub">Time until first word appears. 1–2s feels instant for most business tools. Interactive chat: &lt;1s.</span>
          <input type="number" id="ttft" value="2" min="0.1" max="60" step="0.1" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label class="field-label">Max total time for the reply (TTLT), in seconds</label>
          <span class="field-sub">Total time for full response. Long documents may take 30–120s even on good hardware.</span>
          <input type="number" id="ttlt" value="30" min="1" max="600" step="1" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="warn-box text-xs">
        ⚠️ The guide notes: tighter speed limits cut how much the system can do at once. These are planning targets — check your GPU's real benchmarks before you buy.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card mb-5">
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-brand-forest mb-1">Do you also train the AI on your own data?</h3>
      <p class="text-brand-muted text-sm mb-4">Training teaches the AI your company's documents, style, or domain. It needs much more memory than just running it, but only while training runs. The guide's table shows the exact memory needed.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-2">
        <button class="choice-btn sel" data-action="selMode" data-mode="inference">
          <div class="ct">✓ Inference only — just run the AI</div>
          <div class="cd">Use the model as-is. Most common. No extra memory needed.</div>
        </button>
        <button class="choice-btn" data-action="selMode" data-mode="qlora4">
          <div class="ct">Train with QLoRA 4-bit (most memory-efficient)</div>
          <div class="cd">Uses about 93% less memory than full training. Good quality. Best for tight budgets.</div>
        </button>
        <button class="choice-btn" data-action="selMode" data-mode="qlora8">
          <div class="ct">Train with QLoRA 8-bit</div>
          <div class="cd">Uses about 87% less memory than full training. Better quality than 4-bit.</div>
        </button>
        <button class="choice-btn" data-action="selMode" data-mode="lora">
          <div class="ct">Train with LoRA 16-bit</div>
          <div class="cd">Uses about 78% less memory than full training. High quality.</div>
        </button>
        <button class="choice-btn" data-action="selMode" data-mode="full">
          <div class="ct">Train fully (16-bit)</div>
          <div class="cd">Best quality. Needs a lot of memory. For expert AI teams only.</div>
        </button>
      </div>
      <div id="ftNotSupported" class="warn-box mt-3 text-xs hidden">
        ⚠️ The guide's training table only covers 7B, 13B, 30B, 70B, and 110B models. We don't estimate training memory for this size, to avoid guessing.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:justify-between gap-3 mt-4">
      <button class="btn-ghost" data-action="goStep" data-step="3">← Back</button>
      <button class="btn-primary" data-action="goStep" data-step="5">Next: your GPUs and results →</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- STEP 5 -->
  <div id="step5" class="hidden fade-in">
    <div class="card mb-5">
      <p class="sec-hdr">Your GPUs</p>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-forest mb-1">Add your GPUs</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-muted text-sm mb-5">Pick from the list or enter your own. We'll show how many GPUs you need and, once you add prices, what it costs to run per million prompts.</p>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <label class="field-label">Pick from GPU catalog</label>
        <span class="field-sub">Includes datacenter, workstation, and consumer GPUs from NVIDIA, AMD, and Intel. The memory figures come from official specs. Add more than one to compare.</span>
<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-2">
            <div class="flex-1 relative min-w-0">
              <select id="gpuCatalogSelect" class="pr-9 w-full">
              <option value="">— Choose a GPU to add —</option>
            </select>
            <span class="absolute right-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 pointer-events-none text-brand-muted">▾</span>
          </div>
          <button class="btn-primary" style="padding:11px 18px;white-space:nowrap;" data-action="addFromCatalog">+ Add</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <div class="flex-1 h-px bg-brand-forest/10"></div>
        <span class="text-brand-muted text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">or add your own GPU</span>
        <div class="flex-1 h-px bg-brand-forest/10"></div>
      </div>
      <button class="btn-sm mb-5" data-action="addGpuRow">+ Add a GPU manually</button>

      <div id="gpuTableWrap" class="hidden gpu-table-container">
        <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-2">
          <table id="gpuTable">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th style="min-width:200px">GPU name</th>
                <th style="min-width:110px">Memory per GPU (GB)</th>
                <th style="min-width:160px">Price per GPU (optional)</th>
                <th style="min-width:160px">Yearly opex per GPU (optional)</th>
                <th style="width:36px"></th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="gpuBody"></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="note">Yearly opex = power + space + upkeep for each GPU. Add price and opex to see your cost per prompt.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="resultsSection"></div>

    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:justify-between gap-3 mt-4">
      <button class="btn-ghost" data-action="goStep" data-step="4">← Back</button>
      <button class="btn-primary" data-action="resetAll">↺ Start Over</button>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<script>
  import '../scripts/llm-calculator/main.ts';
</script>
